    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d272">

                <pb facs="0395" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg307"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Porter to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-05-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 30,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Porter advises that he has complied with Department’s instructions of the
                    28th instant, and that the minister for foreign <pb facs="0396" n="308"
                        xml:id="pg308"/> affairs at once instructed the French minister at Tangier
                    to cooperate by all possible means in the rescue of Perdicaris, to urge the
                    Sultan to action, and to engage the services of certain religious families of
                    influence who have heretofore been useful in similar affairs.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
